# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT: console key material.
#
# tools/hactool/prod.keys is 14,612 bytes of Nintendo Switch master keys and
# was sitting inside tools/, which the ignore rules above did not exclude. A
# blanket `git add -A` would have staged and pushed it. Treat any file matching
# these patterns as radioactive -- if one is already tracked, rotating the keys
# is the only remediation, so check with `git ls-files | grep -i keys` before
# ever publishing.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.keys
**/prod.keys
**/title.keys*
**/dev.keys
keys/
**/keys/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT: decrypted game code and the external tooling that produced it.
#
# exefs/ is 5.7 GB of decrypted Nintendo NSO binaries plus a third-party
# recompiler tree. It is Nintendo's copyrighted code and it is not this
# project's source. It is fully regenerable from a user's own legally
# obtained dump, so it stays out of the repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
exefs/

# decomp/script/*.pasm is the intermediate assembly form of the 691 decompiled
# battle scripts; the *.pseudo.c files beside them are the actual deliverable
# and ARE tracked (33 MB, 691 scripts). Only the regenerable .pasm is dropped.
decomp/script/*.pasm
decomp/*/build*/

# Runtime autosaves produced by the verification binaries
**/save_data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build artifacts and third-party binaries. Nothing binary belongs in this
# repository: the project is source, and every one of these is either compiled
# by our own tools or downloaded by the user.
#
# tools/shim/{less,pager_shim,tail}.exe are three copies of the same 118 KB
# binary built from tools/shim/pager_shim.c -- diff.py prepends tools/shim to
# PATH so Windows resolves `less`/`tail` to it. The .py and .cmd sources beside
# them are tracked; the .exe and .obj are not.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.obj
tools/shim/*.exe
tools/hactool/hactool.exe
